{"model": "devstral-small-2:latest", "created_at": "2026-10-21T21:18:47.16412572Z", "response": "Let's solve each problem step by step.\n\n### Problem 1:\nMaria buys 7 notebooks at $4 each and 12 pens at $1.50 each.\nCost of notebooks = 7 * 4 = $28\nCost of pens = 12 * 1.50 = $18\nTotal cost = 28 + 18 = $46\nWith a 10% discount: 46 * 0.90 = $41.40\n\nANSWER 1: $41.40\n\n### Problem 2:\nLet Cara's current age be C.\nBen is twice as old as Cara was 6 years ago: Ben = 2*(C - 6)\nIn 4 years, Ben will be 30: Ben + 4 = 30 => Ben = 26\nSo, 2*(C - 6) = 26 => C - 6 = 13 => C = 19\n\nANSWER 2: 19\n\n### Problem 3:\nFrom the clues:\n- Alice does not own the fish (so Alice owns cat or dog).\n- The dog owner drinks coffee.\n- Ben drinks juice.\n- Cleo does not drink tea (so Cleo drinks coffee or juice).\n\nPossible assignments:\n- Ben drinks juice, so Ben does not drink coffee. Thus, the dog owner must be Alice or Cleo.\n- Cleo does not drink tea, so Cleo drinks coffee or juice. But Ben drinks juice, so Cleo drinks coffee.\n- Thus, Cleo owns the dog (since she drinks coffee).\n- Alice does not own the fish, so Alice owns the cat.\n- Ben owns the fish.\n\nANSWER 3: Cleo owns the dog, Ben owns the fish\n\n### Problem 4:\nThe sequence is: 2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?\nDifferences between terms: 4, 6, 8, 10\nNext difference: 12\nNext term: 30 + 12 = 42\n\nANSWER 4: 42\n\n### Problem 5:\nAll but 9 sheep die: 17 - 9 = 8 sheep left.\n\nANSWER 5: 8\n\n### Problem 6:\nPipe A fills the tank in 6 hours, so rate = 1/6 tank per hour.\nPipe B fills the tank in 3 hours, so rate = 1/3 tank per hour.\nCombined rate = 1/6 + 1/3 = 1/2 tank per hour.\nTime to fill the tank = 1 / (1/2) = 2 hours.\n\nANSWER 6: 2\n\n### Problem 7:\nA kilogram of feathers and a pound of steel are both 1 kg (since 1 pound \u2248 0.45 kg), so they weigh the same.\n\nANSWER 7: They weigh the same\n\n### Problem 8:\nLet original cost be C.\nRetail price = C + 25% of C = 1.25C\nSale price = 1.25C - 20% of 1.25C = 1.25C * 0.80 = C\nSale price is 100% of the original cost.\n\nANSWER 8: 100%\n\n### Problem 9:\nX says: \"At least one of us is a liar.\"\n- If X is a truth-teller, then at least one of X or Y is a liar. But X is a truth-teller, so Y must be a liar.\n- If X is a liar, then the statement \"At least one of us is a liar\" is false, meaning neither X nor Y is a liar. But this contradicts X being a liar.\nThus, X must be a truth-teller, and Y is a liar.\n\nANSWER 9: X is a truth-teller, Y is a liar\n\n### Problem 10:\n3x + 7 = 2x + 15\n3x - 2x = 15 - 7\nx = 8\n\nANSWER 10: 8\n\n### Problem 11:\nNumber of ways to choose 3 people from 5 is C(5, 3) = 10.\n\nANSWER 11: 10\n\n### Problem 12:\nDan is taller than Ellie.\nEllie is shorter than Farah.\nFarah is shorter than Dan.\nThus, Dan is the tallest, and Ellie is the shortest.\n\nANSWER 12: Dan is the tallest, Ellie is the shortest", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "context": [17, 4568, 1584, 12056, 126744, 5624, 53721, 1045, 1050, 1045, 1050, 1052, 1066, 47926, 8166, 1045, 1050, 1053, 1049, 1050, 1044, 1261, 43520, 26242, 11512, 1319, 23947, 1077, 1041, 6254, 1536, 42301, 2784, 26554, 1044, 1261, 8689, 53862, 3518, 125609, 1294, 6993, 1626, 4568, 4053, 1420, 26554, 27089, 4418, 2301, 38680, 1626, 16994, 7807, 4469, 1486, 3804, 12220, 1408, 1032, 1050, 1048, 1050, 1051, 1045, 1049, 1048, 1045, 1048, 1049, 1626, 1784, 3519, 5451, 1395, 1032, 1050, 1048, 1050, 1054, 1045, 1049, 1048, 1045, 1050, 1049, 1338, 7651, 1636, 6185, 1605, 5257, 2314, 2269, 3686, 1505, 2200, 1278, 3330, 1681, 4546, 10867, 2015, 6793, 43546, 1505, 4811, 2181, 1044, 1636, 4016, 2210, 1278, 5178, 12589, 1317, 15273, 1278, 3686, 1046, 5469, 1605, 89786, 1317, 2210, 12589, 26119, 2127, 1710, 5234, 1261, 2081, 18501, 1505, 7662, 4005, 1046, 3367, 1836, 11157, 12589, 1584, 5178, 1044, 2430, 11904, 3468, 1455, 1636, 2607, 2405, 1736, 1278, 3686, 1321, 10035, 6187, 2015, 7211, 1626, 5475, 1278, 3330, 1681, 4098, 1395, 1605, 6133, 1044, 61103, 1044, 1505, 3120, 1605, 5234, 61